{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Imam Ali (a.s.) on the Mab'ath — Najaf",
  "data": "On the night or the day of the Mab'ath, stand at the gate of the dome, facing the tomb of Imam Ali (a.s.), and say:\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any associate.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUH\nAnd I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger,\nوَاَنَّ عَلِيَّ بْنَ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَبْدُ اللّٰهِ وَاَخُوْ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nWA ANNA A'LIYYABNA ABEE TAALIBIN AMEERAL MU'MINEENA A'BDULLAAHI WA AKHOO RASOOLIH\nand that ‘Ali the son of Abu-Talib, the Commander of the Faithful, is the servant of Allah and the brother of His Messenger,\nوَاَنَّ الْاَئِمَّةَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ مِنْ وُلْدِهٖ حُجَجُ اللّٰهِ عَلٰى خَلْقِهٖ\nWA ANNAL A'IMMATAT TAAHIREENA MIN WULDIHEE HUJAJULLAAHI A'LAA KHALQIH\nand that the immaculate Imams from his offspring are Allah’s arguments against His creatures.\nThen enter, stand at the tomb facing it, with the qiblah between your shoulders, and say 100 times:\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBAR\nAllah is the Most Great.\nAfter the takbir, say:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اٰدَمَ خَلِيْفَةِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA AADAMA KHALEEFATILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Adam the vicegerent of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ نُوْحٍ صِفْوَةِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA NOOHIN SIFWATILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Noah the choice of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Abraham the intimate friend of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُوْسٰى كَلِيْمِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA MOOSAA KALEEMILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Moses the spoken by Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عِيْسٰى رُوْحِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA I'EESAA ROOHILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Jesus the spirit of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُحَمَّدٍ سَيِّدِ رُسُلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA MUHAMMADIN SAYYIDI RUSULILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of Muhammad the chief of Allah’s Messengers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AMEERAL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon you, O Commander of the Faithful.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اِمَامَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA IMAAMAL MUTTAQEEN\nPeace be upon you, O epitome of the pious ones.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا سَيِّدَ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAYYIDAL WASIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O chief of the Prophets’ successors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَصِيَّ رَسُوْلِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WASIYYA RASOOLI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O successor of the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عِلْمِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA I'LMIL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN\nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of the knowledge of the past and the coming generations.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا النَّبَاُ الْعَظِيْمُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAN NABA'UL A'ZEEM\nPeace be upon you, O Great News.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الصِّرَاطُ الْمُسْتَقِيْمُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAS SIRAATUL MUSTAQEEM\nPeace be upon you, O Straight Path.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْمُهَذَّبُ الْكَرِيْمُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL MUHADHDHABUL KAREEM\nPeace be upon you, O noble, refined one.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْوَصِيُّ التَّقِيُّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL WASIYYUT TAQIYY\nPeace be upon you, O pious successor (of the Prophet).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الرَّضِيُّ الزَّكِيُّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAR RADIYYUZ ZAKIYY\nPeace be upon you, O well-pleased, pure one.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْبَدْرُ الْمُضِيْءُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL BADRUL MUDEE'\nPeace be upon you, O shining full moon.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الصِّدِّيْقُ الْاَكْبَرُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAS SIDDEEQUL AKBAR\nPeace be upon you, O grandest veracious one.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْفَارُوْقُ الْاَعْظَمُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL FAAROOQUL A'ZAM\nPeace be upon you, O greatest distinguisher (between the right and the wrong).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا السِّرَاجُ الْمُنِيْرُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAS SIRAAJUL MUNEER\nPeace be upon you, O glowing lantern.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اِمَامَ الْهُدٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA IMAAMAL HUDAA\nPeace be upon you, O leader to the true guidance.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَلَمَ التُّقٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'LAMAT TUQAA\nPeace be upon you, O pattern of piety.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ الْكُبْرٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HUJJATALLAAHIL KUBRAA\nPeace be upon you, O grand argument of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَآصَّةَ اللّٰهِ وَخَالِصَتَهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAASSATALLAAHI WA KHAALISATAH\nPeace be upon you, O select and elite of Allah,\nوَاَمِيْنَ اللّٰهِ وَصَفْوَتَهٗ\nWA AMEENALLAAHI WA SAFWATAH\ntrustee and choice of Allah,\nوَبَابَ اللّٰهِ وَحُجَّتَهٗ\nWA BAABALLAAHI WA HUJJATAH\ndoor to and argument of Allah,\nوَمَعْدِنَ حُكْمِ اللّٰهِ وَسِرِّهٖ\nWA MA'DINA HUKMILLAAHI WA SIRRIH\nsource and secret of Allah’s judgment,\nوَعَيْبَةَ عِلْمِ اللّٰهِ وَخَازِنَهٗ\nWA A'YBATA I'LMILLAAHI WA KHAAZINAH\nguardian and keeper of Allah’s knowledge,\nوَسَفِيْرَ اللّٰهِ فِيْ خَلْقِهٖ\nWA SAFEERALLAAHI FEE KHALQIH\nand envoy of Allah among His creatures.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلَاةَ وَاٰتَيْتَ الزَّكَاةَ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA AQAMTAS SALAATA WA AATAYTAZ ZAKAAH\nI bear witness that you performed the prayers and paid the zakat,\nوَاَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَنَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ\nWA AMARTA BIL MA'ROOFI WA NAHAYTA A'NIL MUNKAR\nenjoined the right and forbade the wrong,\nوَاتَّبَعْتَ الرَّسُوْلَ وَتَلَوْتَ الْكِتَابَ حَقَّ تِلَاوَتِهٖ\nWATTABA'TAR RASOOLA WA TALAWTAL KITAABA HAQQA TILAAWATIH\nfollowed the Messenger, recited the Book as exactly as it must be recited,\nوَبَلَّغْتَ عَنِ اللّٰهِ وَوَفَيْتَ بِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ\nWA BALLAGHTA A'NILLAAHI WA WAFAYTA BI-A'HDILLAAH\nconveyed the messages of Allah, fulfilled your covenant with Allah,\nوَتَمَّتْ بِكَ كَلِمَاتُ اللّٰهِ\nWA TAMMAT BIKA KALIMAATULLAAH\nthe Words of Allah were accomplished by you,\nوَجَاهَدْتَ فِي اللّٰهِ حَقَّ جِهَادِهٖ\nWA JAAHADTA FILLAAHI HAQQA JIHAADIH\nstrove in Allah’s way in the best manner,\nوَنَصَحْتَ لِلّٰهِ وَلِرَسُوْلِهٖ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nWA NASAHTA LILLAAHI WA LIRASOOLIHEE SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nadvised for the sake of Allah and for the sake of His Messenger, peace be upon him and his Household,\nوَجُدْتَ بِنَفْسِكَ صَابِرًا مُحْتَسِبًا\nWA JUDTA BINAFSIKA SAABIRAN MUHTASIBAA\nand sacrificed yourself with steadfastness, seeking Allah’s reward,\nمُجَاهِدًا عَنْ دِيْنِ اللّٰهِ مُوَقِّيًا لِرَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nMUJAAHIDAN A'N DEENILLAAHI MUWAQQIYAN LIRASOOLILLAAH\nstruggling for the defense of Allah’s religion, protecting Allah’s Messenger,\nطَالِبًا مَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ رَاغِبًا فِيْمَا وَعَدَ اللّٰهُ\nTAALIBAN MAA I'NDALLAAHI RAAGHIBAN FEEMAA WA'ADALLAAH\nseeking for that which is with Allah, and desiring for that which Allah has promised.\nوَمَضَيْتَ لِلَّذِيْ كُنْتَ عَلَيْهِ شَهِيْدًا وَشَاهِدًا وَمَشْهُوْدًا\nWA MADAYTA LILLADHEE KUNTA A'LAYHI SHAHEEDAN WA SHAAHIDAN WA MASH-HOODAA\nYou also sealed your life as martyr, a witness, and witnessed;\nفَجَزَاكَ اللّٰهُ عَنْ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nFAJAZAAKALLAAHU A'N RASOOLIH\nso, may Allah reward you on behalf of His Messenger,\nوَعَنِ الْاِسْلَامِ وَاَهْلِهٖ مِنْ صِدِّيْقٍ اَفْضَلَ الْجَزَاۤءِ\nWA A'NIL ISLAAMI WA AHLIHEE MIN SIDDEEQIN AFDALAL JAZAA'\nIslam, and the people of Islam with the most favorite reward, for you are veracious.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ كُنْتَ اَوَّلَ الْقَوْمِ اِسْلَامًا\nASH-HADU ANNAKA KUNTA AWWALAL QAWMI ISLAAMAA\nI bear witness that you were the first to embrace Islam,\nوَاَخْلَصَهُمْ اِيْمَانًا وَاَشَدَّهُمْ يَقِيْنًا\nWA AKHLASAHUM EEMAANAN WA ASHADDAHUM YAQEENAA\nthe most sincere in faith, the most confident,\nوَاَخْوَفَهُمْ لِلّٰهِ وَاَعْظَمَهُمْ عَنَاۤءً\nWA AKHWAFAHUM LILLAAHI WA A'ZAMAHUM A'NAA'AA\nthe most Allah-fearing, the most steadfast (against ordeals for the sake of Islam),\nوَاَحْوَطَهُمْ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nWA AHWATAHUM A'LAA RASOOLILLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nthe most watchful for Allah’s Messenger, peace be upon him and his Household,\nوَاَفْضَلَهُمْ مَنَاقِبَ وَاَكْثَرَهُمْ سَوَابِقَ\nWA AFDALAHUM MANAAQIBA WA AKTHARAHUM SAWAABIQ\nendowed with the most favorable merits, the foremost of everyone else in everything,\nوَاَرْفَعَهُمْ دَرَجَةً وَاَشْرَفَهُمْ مَنْزِلَةً\nWA ARFA'AHUM DARAJATAN WA ASHRAFAHUM MANZILAH\nthe owner of the most elevated rank, the owner of the most honorable position,\nوَاَكْرَمَهُمْ عَلَيْهِ فَقَوِيْتَ حِيْنَ وَهَنُوْا\nWA AKRAMAHUM A'LAYHI FAQAWEETA HEENA WAHANOO\nand the most respected by him. Thus, you became stronger when they became weak,\nوَلَزِمْتَ مِنْهَاجَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nWA LAZIMTA MINHAAJA RASOOLILLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nand you abode by the course of Allah’s Messenger, peace be upon him and his Household.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ كُنْتَ خَلِيْفَتَهٗ حَقًّا لَمْ تُنَازَعْ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNAKA KUNTA KHALEEFATAHOO HAQQAN LAM TUNAAZA'\nI also bear witness that you were the true vicegerent of him (i.e. the Holy Prophet); no one could ever compete with you in this position\nبِرَغْمِ الْمُنَافِقِيْنَ وَغَيْظِ الْكَافِرِيْنَ وَضِغْنِ الْفَاسِقِيْنَ\nBIRAGHMIL MUNAAFIQEENA WA GHAYZIL KAAFIREENA WA DIGHNIL FAASIQEEN\nin spite of the existence of hypocrites, the despise of the unbelievers, and the malice of the wicked.\nوَقُمْتَ بِالْاَمْرِ حِيْنَ فَشِلُوْا\nWA QUMTA BIL AMRI HEENA FASHILOO\nYou also managed the matters when they failed to do so,\nوَنَطَقْتَ حِيْنَ تَتَعْتَعُوْا\nWA NATAQTA HEENA TATA'TA'OO\nyou spoke (the truth) when they stammered,\nوَمَضَيْتَ بِنُوْرِ اللّٰهِ اِذْ وَقَفُوْا\nWA MADAYTA BINOORILLAAHI IDH WAQAFOO\nand you carried on with the light of Allah when they stopped.\nفَمَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ فَقَدِ اهْتَدٰى\nFAMANIT TABA'AKA FAQADIH TADAA\nHence, he who follows you has actually been led to the true guidance.\nكُنْتَ اَوَّلَهُمْ كَلَامًا وَاَشَدَّهُمْ خِصَامًا\nKUNTA AWWALAHUM KALAAMAN WA ASHADDAHUM KHISAAMAA\nYou were the first to speak, the firmest in refuting the rivals,\nوَاَصْوَبَهُمْ مَنْطِقًا وَاَسَدَّهُمْ رَاْيًا\nWA ASWABAHUM MANTIQAN WA ASADDAHUM RA'YAA\nthe most eloquent of them, the most apposite in opinions,\nوَاَشْجَعَهُمْ قَلْبًا وَاَكْثَرَهُمْ يَقِيْنًا\nWA ASHJA'AHUM QALBAN WA AKTHARAHUM YAQEENAA\nthe most courageous, the most confident of them,\nوَاَحْسَنَهُمْ عَمَلًا وَاَعْرَفَهُمْ بِالْاُمُوْرِ\nWA AHSANAHUM A'MALAN WA A'RAFAHUM BIL UMOOR\nthe best of them in deeds, and the most learned in affairs.\nكُنْتَ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَبًا رَحِيْمًا\nKUNTA LIL MU'MINEENA ABAN RAHEEMAA\nFor the believers, you were a merciful father,\nاِذْ صَارُوْا عَلَيْكَ عِيَالًا\nIDH SAAROO A'LAYKA I'YAALAA\nwhen they became your dependants;\nفَحَمَلْتَ اَثْقَالَ مَا عَنْهُ ضَعُفُوْا\nFAHAMALTA ATHQAALA MAA A'NHU DA'UFOO\nso, you carried the burdens that they were too weak to carry,\nوَحَفِظْتَ مَاۤ اَضَاعُوْا\nWA HAFIZTA MAA ADAA'OO\npreserved that which they forfeited,\nوَرَعَيْتَ مَاۤ اَهْمَلُوْا\nWA RA'AYTA MAA AHMALOO\nconserved that which they neglected,\nوَشَمَّرْتَ اِذْ جَبَنُوْا\nWA SHAMMARTA IDH JABANOO\nprepared yourself for facing that which they were too coward to face,\nوَعَلَوْتَ اِذْ هَلِعُوْا\nWA A'LAWTA IDH HALI'OO\nadvanced when they were dismayed,\nوَصَبَرْتَ اِذْ جَزِعُوْا\nWA SABARTA IDH JAZI'OO\nand acted steadfastly when they became anxious.\nكُنْتَ عَلَى الْكَافِرِيْنَ عَذَابًا صَبًّا وَغِلْظَةً وَغَيْظًا\nKUNTA A'LAL KAAFIREENA A'DHAABAN SABBAN WA GHILZATAN WA GHAYZAA\nYou were thus incessant torment on the unbelievers, and you were also rude and furious (on them).\nوَلِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ غَيْثًا وَخِصْبًا وَعِلْمًا\nWA LIL MU'MINEENA GHAYTHAN WA KHISBAN WA I'LMAA\nYou rained (with mercy) on the believers, and you were fertile and source of knowledge for them.\nلَمْ تُفْلَلْ حُجَّتُكَ وَلَمْ يَزِغْ قَلْبُكَ\nLAM TUFLAL HUJJATUKA WA LAM YAZIGH QALBUK\nYour argument was never weak, your heart never deviated,\nوَلَمْ تَضْعُفْ بَصِيْرَتُكَ وَلَمْ تَجْبُنْ نَفْسُكَ\nWA LAM TAD'UF BASEERATUKA WA LAM TAJBUN NAFSUK\nyour sagacity was never feeble, and your determination never cowered.\nكُنْتَ كَالْجَبَلِ لَا تُحَرِّكُهُ الْعَوَاصِفُ\nKUNTA KAL JABALI LAA TUHARRIKUHUL A'WAASIF\nYou were as firm as a mountain, since storms could never displace you\nوَلَا تُزِيْلُهُ الْقَوَاصِفُ\nWA LAA TUZEELUHUL QAWAASIF\nand misfortunes could never move you.\nكُنْتَ كَمَا قَالَ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nKUNTA KAMAA QAALA RASOOLULLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nYou were as exactly as described by Allah’s Messenger, peace be upon him and his Household, who said about you that you are\nقَوِيًّا فِيْ بَدَنِكَ مُتَوَاضِعًا فِيْ نَفْسِكَ\nQAWIYYAN FEE BADANIKA MUTAWAADI'AN FEE NAFSIK\nstrong in your body, modest in yourself,\nعَظِيْمًا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ كَبِيْرًا فِي الْاَرْضِ\nA'ZEEMAN I'NDALLAAHI KABEERAN FIL ARD\ngreat in the view of Allah, imposing in the earth,\nجَلِيْلًا فِي السَّمَاۤءِ\nJALEELAN FIS SAMAA'\nand lofty in the heavens.\nلَمْ يَكُنْ لِاَحَدٍ فِيْكَ مَهْمَزٌ\nLAM YAKUN LI-AHADIN FEEKA MAHMAZ\nNone could ever find fault with you,\nوَلَا لِقَاۤئِلٍ فِيْكَ مَغْمَزٌ\nWA LAA LIQAA'ILIN FEEKA MAGHMAZ\nnone could ever speak evil of you,\nوَلَا لِخَلْقٍ فِيْكَ مَطْمَعٌ\nWA LAA LIKHALQIN FEEKA MATMA'\nno creature could ever hope to sway you,\nوَلَا لِاَحَدٍ عِنْدَكَ هَوَادَةٌ\nWA LAA LI-AHADIN I'NDAKA HAWAADAH\nand you were never lenient (unfairly) to anyone.\nيُوْجَدُ الضَّعِيْفُ الذَّلِيْلُ عِنْدَكَ قَوِيًّا عَزِيْزًا\nYOOJADUD DA'EEFUDH DHALEELU I'NDAKA QAWIYYAN A'ZEEZAA\nThe weak, humble one was strong and mighty in your view\nحَتّٰى تَاْخُذَ لَهٗ بِحَقِّهٖ\nHATTAA TA'KHUDHA LAHOO BIHAQQIH\nuntil you took back his right for him,\nوَالْقَوِيُّ الْعَزِيْزُ عِنْدَكَ ضَعِيْفًا\nWAL QAWIYYUL A'ZEEZU I'NDAKA DA'EEFAA\nand the strong, mighty one was weak in your view\nحَتّٰى تَاْخُذَ مِنْهُ الْحَقَّ\nHATTAA TA'KHUDHA MINHUL HAQQ\nuntil you took the others’ rights from him.\nالْقَرِيْبُ وَالْبَعِيْدُ عِنْدَكَ فِيْ ذٰلِكَ سَوَاۤءٌ\nAL-QAREEBU WAL BA'EEDU I'NDAKA FEE DHAALIKA SAWAA'\nThe near and the remote were equal in your view.\nشَاْنُكَ الْحَقُّ وَالصِّدْقُ وَالرِّفْقُ\nSHA'NUKAL HAQQU WAS SIDQU WAR RIFQ\nYour habit was to be true, honest, and kind,\nوَقَوْلُكَ حُكْمٌ وَحَتْمٌ\nWA QAWLUKA HUKMUN WA HATM\nyour words were ruling and determination,\nوَاَمْرُكَ حِلْمٌ وَعَزْمٌ\nWA AMRUKA HILMUN WA A'ZM\nyour custom was forbearance and fortitude,\nوَرَاْيُكَ عِلْمٌ وَحَزْمٌ\nWA RA'YUKA I'LMUN WA HAZM\nand your view was knowledge and firmness.\nاِعْتَدَلَ بِكَ الدِّيْنُ\nI'TADALA BIKAD DEEN\nAt your hands, the religion became even,\nوَسَهُلَ بِكَ الْعَسِيْرُ\nWA SAHULA BIKAL A'SEER\nthe difficult became easy,\nوَاُطْفِئَتْ بِكَ النِّيْرَانُ\nWA UTFI'AT BIKAN NEERAAN\nthe fires were extinguished,\nوَقَوِيَ بِكَ الْاِيْمَانُ\nWA QAWIYA BIKAL EEMAAN\nthe faith became strong,\nوَثَبَتَ بِكَ الْاِسْلَامُ\nWA THABATA BIKAL ISLAAM\nIslam became steady,\nوَهَدَّتْ مُصِيْبَتُكَ الْاَنَامَ\nWA HADDAT MUSEEBATUKAL ANAAM\nand the calamity of losing you undermined all people.\nفَاِنَّا لِلّٰهِ وَاِنَّا اِلَيْهِ رَاجِعُوْنَ\nFA-INNAA LILLAAHI WA INNAA ILAYHI RAAJI'OON\nSurely, we are Allah's and to Him we shall surely return.\nلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ قَتَلَكَ\nLA'ANALLAAHU MAN QATALAK\nCurse of Allah be upon him who slew you,\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ خَالَفَكَ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MAN KHAALAFAK\ncurse of Allah be upon him who mutinied against you,\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَيْكَ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MANIF TARAA A'LAYK\ncurse of Allah be upon him who forged lies against you,\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ ظَلَمَكَ وَغَصَبَكَ حَقَّكَ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MAN ZALAMAKA WA GHASABAKA HAQQAK\ncurse of Allah be upon him who wronged you and usurped your right,\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ بَلَغَهٗ ذٰلِكَ فَرَضِيَ بِهٖ\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU MAN BALAGHAHOO DHAALIKA FARADIYA BIH\nand curse of Allah be upon him who, when informed of this, was pleased with it.\nاِنَّا اِلَى اللّٰهِ مِنْهُمْ بُرَاۤءُ\nINNAA ILALLAAHI MINHUM BURAA'\nVerily, before Allah we disavow them.\nلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ اُمَّةً خَالَفَتْكَ\nLA'ANALLAAHU UMMATAN KHAALAFATK\nCurse of Allah be upon the group that disagreed with you,\nوَجَحَدَتْ وِلَايَتَكَ\nWA JAHADAT WILAAYATAK\ndenied your (Divinely commissioned) leadership,\nوَتَظَاهَرَتْ عَلَيْكَ وَقَتَلَتْكَ\nWA TAZAAHARAT A'LAYKA WA QATALATK\naided each other against you, slew you,\nوَحَادَتْ عَنْكَ وَخَذَلَتْكَ\nWA HAADAT A'NKA WA KHADHALATK\ndeviated from you, and disappointed you.\nالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ جَعَلَ النَّارَ مَثْوَاهُمْ\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE JA'ALAN NAARA MATHWAAHUM\nAll praise be to Allah Who has made Hellfire their abode,\nوَبِئْسَ الْوِرْدُ الْمَوْرُوْدُ\nWA BI'SAL WIRDUL MAWROOD\nand evil the place to which they are brought.\nاَشْهَدُ لَكَ يَا وَلِيَّ اللّٰهِ\nASH-HADU LAKA YAA WALIYYALLAAH\nI bear witness for you, O intimate servant of Allah\nوَوَلِيَّ رَسُوْلِهٖ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ بِالْبَلَاغِ وَالْاَدَاۤءِ\nWA WALIYYA RASOOLIHEE SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE BIL BALAAGHI WAL ADAA'\nand loyalist of Allah’s Messenger, peace be upon him and his Household, that you did convey and carry out (your mission).\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ حَبِيْبُ اللّٰهِ وَبَابُهٗ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNAKA HABEEBULLAAHI WA BAABUH\nAnd I bear witness that you are the beloved of Allah and the door to Him,\nوَاَنَّكَ جَنْبُ اللّٰهِ وَوَجْهُهُ الَّذِيْ مِنْهُ يُؤْتٰى\nWA ANNAKA JANBULLAAHI WA WAJHUHUL LADHEE MINHU YU'TAA\nyou are the Side of Allah and His Face from which one can come to Allah,\nوَاَنَّكَ سَبِيْلُ اللّٰهِ وَاَنَّكَ عَبْدُ اللّٰهِ\nWA ANNAKA SABEELULLAAHI WA ANNAKA A'BDULLAAH\nyou are Allah’s way, you are Allah’s servant,\nوَاَخُوْ رَسُوْلِهٖ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nWA AKHOO RASOOLIHEE SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nand you are the brother of His Messenger, peace be upon him and his Household.\nاَتَيْتُكَ زَاۤئِرًا لِعَظِيْمِ حَالِكَ\nATAYTUKA ZAA'IRAN LI-A'ZEEMI HAALIK\nI have thus come to visit you because you enjoy a magnificent position\nوَمَنْزِلَتِكَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَعِنْدَ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nWA MANZILATIKA I'NDALLAAHI WA I'NDA RASOOLIH\nand standing with Allah and with His Messenger.\nمُتَقَرِّبًا اِلَى اللّٰهِ بِزِيَارَتِكَ\nMUTAQARRIBAN ILALLAAHI BIZIYAARATIK\nSo, I seek nearness to Allah through my visit to you\nرَاغِبًا اِلَيْكَ فِي الشَّفَاعَةِ\nRAAGHIBAN ILAYKA FISH SHAFAA'AH\nand I desire that you will intercede for me.\nاَبْتَغِيْ بِشَفَاعَتِكَ خَلَاصَ نَفْسِيْ\nABTAGHEE BISHAFAA'ATIKA KHALAASA NAFSEE\nThrough your intercession for me, I hope for redemption of myself,\nمُتَعَوِّذًا بِكَ مِنَ النَّارِ\nMUTA'AWWIDHAN BIKA MINAN NAAR\nI seek refuge with you against Hellfire,\nهَارِبًا مِنْ ذُنُوْبِيَ الَّتِي احْتَطَبْتُهَا عَلٰى ظَهْرِيْ\nHAARIBAN MIN DHUNOOBIYAL LATIH TATABTUHAA A'LAA ZAHREE\nI am fleeing from my sins that I have overburdened myself with,\nفَزِعًا اِلَيْكَ رَجَاۤءَ رَحْمَةِ رَبِّيْ\nFAZI'AN ILAYKA RAJAA'A RAHMATI RABBEE\nand I resort to you in the hope of my Lord’s mercy.\nاَتَيْتُكَ اَسْتَشْفِعُ بِكَ يَا مَوْلَايَ اِلَى اللّٰهِ\nATAYTUKA ASTASHFI'U BIKA YAA MAWLAAYA ILALLAAH\nI have come to you, O my master, seeking your intercession for me before Allah\nوَاَتَقَرَّبُ بِكَ اِلَيْهِ لِيَقْضِيَ بِكَ حَوَاۤئِجِيْ\nWA ATAQARRABU BIKA ILAYHI LIYAQDIYA BIKA HAWAA'IJEE\nand seeking nearness to Him through you so that He may settle my needs;\nفَاشْفَعْ لِيْ يَاۤ اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اِلَى اللّٰهِ\nFASHFA' LEE YAA AMEERAL MU'MINEENA ILALLAAH\nso, (please) intercede for me, O Commander of the Faithful.\nفَاِنِّيْ عَبْدُ اللّٰهِ وَمَوْلَاكَ وَزَاۤئِرُكَ\nFA-INNEE A'BDULLAAHI WA MAWLAAKA WA ZAA'IRUK\nVerily, I am the slave of Allah and your servant and visitor,\nوَلَكَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الْمَقَامُ الْمَعْلُوْمُ وَالْجَاهُ الْعَظِيْمُ\nWA LAKA I'NDALLAAHIL MAQAAMUL MA'LOOMU WAL JAAHUL A'ZEEM\nand you enjoy a distinguished position with Allah, a great rank,\nوَالشَّاْنُ الْكَبِيْرُ وَالشَّفَاعَةُ الْمَقْبُوْلَةُ\nWASH SHA'NUL KABEERU WASH SHAFAA'ATUL MAQBOOLAH\na big standing, and an admitted right of intercession.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَصَلِّ عَلٰى عَبْدِكَ وَاَمِيْنِكَ الْاَوْفٰى\nWA SALLI A'LAA A'BDIKA WA AMEENIKAL AWFAA\nand send blessings upon Your servant, Your most faithful trustee,\nوَعُرْوَتِكَ الْوُثْقٰى وَيَدِكَ الْعُلْيَا\nWA U'RWATIKAL WUTHQAA WA YADIKAL U'LYAA\nYour firmest handle, Your highest Hand,\nوَكَلِمَتِكَ الْحُسْنٰى وَحُجَّتِكَ عَلَى الْوَرٰى\nWA KALIMATIKAL HUSNAA WA HUJJATIKA A'LAL WARAA\nYour excellent Word, Your argument on the people,\nوَصِدِّيْقِكَ الْاَكْبَرِ سَيِّدِ الْاَوْصِيَاۤءِ\nWA SIDDEEQIKAL AKBARI SAYYIDIL AWSIYAA'\nYour grandest veracious one, the chief of the Prophets’ successors,\nوَرُكْنِ الْاَوْلِيَاۤءِ وَعِمَادِ الْاَصْفِيَاۤءِ\nWA RUKNIL AWLIYAA'I WA I'MAADIL ASFIYAA'\nthe reliance of the saints, the support of the elite ones,\nاَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَيَعْسُوْبِ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ\nAMEERIL MU'MINEENA WA YA'SOOBIL MUTTAQEEN\nthe commander of the faithful, the leader of the pious ones,\nوَقُدْوَةِ الصِّدِّيْقِيْنَ وَاِمَامِ الصَّالِحِيْنَ\nWA QUDWATIS SIDDEEQEENA WA IMAAMIS SAALIHEEN\nthe example of the veracious ones, the pattern of the righteous ones,\nالْمَعْصُوْمِ مِنَ الزَّلَلِ وَالْمَفْطُوْمِ مِنَ الْخَلَلِ\nAL-MA'SOOMI MINAZ ZALALI WAL MAFTOOMI MINAL KHALAL\nthe one protected against flaws, the one saved from defects,\nوَالْمُهَذَّبِ مِنَ الْعَيْبِ وَالْمُطَهَّرِ مِنَ الرَّيْبِ\nWAL MUHADHDHABI MINAL A'YBI WAL MUTAHHARI MINAR RAYB\nthe one cleared from faults, the one purified from doubts,\nاَخِيْ نَبِيِّكَ وَوَصِيِّ رَسُوْلِكَ\nAKHEE NABIYYIKA WA WASIYYI RASOOLIK\nthe brother of Your Prophet, the successor of Your Messenger,\nوَالْبَاۤئِتِ عَلٰى فِرَاشِهٖ وَالْمُوَاسِيْ لَهٗ بِنَفْسِهٖ\nWAL BAA'ITI A'LAA FIRAASHIHEE WAL MUWAASEE LAHOO BINAFSIH\nthe one who replaced him by spending the night on his bed, the one who sacrificed his soul for him,\nوَكَاشِفِ الْكَرْبِ عَنْ وَجْهِهٖ\nWA KAASHIFIL KARBI A'N WAJHIH\nthe one who always relieved him in harsh situations,\nالَّذِيْ جَعَلْتَهٗ سَيْفًا لِنُبُوَّتِهٖ وَمُعْجِزًا لِرِسَالَتِهٖ\nALLADHEE JA'ALTAHOO SAYFAN LINUBUWWATIHEE WA MU'JIZAN LIRISAALATIH\nand the one whom You chose to be the sword of his (i.e. the Prophet’s) Prophethood, the miracle of his (Divine) mission,\nوَدَلَالَةً وَاضِحَةً لِحُجَّتِهٖ\nWA DALAALATAN WAADIHATAN LIHUJJATIH\nthe lucid indication of his arguments,\nوَحَامِلًا لِرَايَتِهٖ وَوِقَايَةً لِمُهْجَتِهٖ\nWA HAAMILAN LIRAAYATIHEE WA WIQAAYATAN LIMUHJATIH\nthe bearer of his pennon, the protector of his soul,\nوَهَادِيًا لِاُمَّتِهٖ وَيَدًا لِبَاْسِهٖ\nWA HAADIYAN LI-UMMATIHEE WA YADAN LIBA'SIH\nthe guide of his nation, the power of his might,\nوَتَاجًا لِرَاْسِهٖ وَبَابًا لِنَصْرِهٖ وَمِفْتَاحًا لِظَفَرِهٖ\nWA TAAJAN LIRA'SIHEE WA BAABAN LINASRIHEE WA MIFTAAHAN LIZAFARIH\nthe crown of his head, the door to his victory, and the key to his triumph,\nحَتّٰى هَزَمَ جُنُوْدَ الشِّرْكِ بِاَيْدِكَ\nHATTAA HAZAMA JUNOODASH SHIRKI BI-AYDIK\nuntil he defeated the armies of polytheism by Your aid,\nوَاَبَادَ عَسَاكِرَ الْكُفْرِ بِاَمْرِكَ\nWA ABAADA A'SAAKIRAL KUFRI BI-AMRIK\nterminated the warriors of atheism by Your permission,\nوَبَذَلَ نَفْسَهٗ فِيْ مَرْضَاتِكَ وَمَرْضَاةِ رَسُوْلِكَ\nWA BADHALA NAFSAHOO FEE MARDAATIKA WA MARDAATI RASOOLIK\nexerted all efforts to win the pleasure of You and Your Messenger,\nوَجَعَلَهَا وَقْفًا عَلٰى طَاعَتِهٖ\nWA JA'ALAHAA WAQFAN A'LAA TAA'ATIH\ndevoted all of his efforts to the obedience to him,\nوَمَجِنًّا دُوْنَ نَكْبَتِهٖ\nWA MAJINNAN DOONA NAKBATIH\nand made of himself armor to protect him from any misfortune,\nحَتّٰى فَاضَتْ نَفْسُهٗ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ فِيْ كَفِّهٖ\nHATTAA FAADAT NAFSUHOO SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE FEE KAFFIH\nuntil the soul of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his Household, departed in the palm of ‘Ali,\nوَاسْتَلَبَ بَرْدَهَا وَمَسَحَهٗ عَلٰى وَجْهِهٖ\nWASTALABA BARDAHAA WA MASAHAHOO A'LAA WAJHIH\nwho thus felt its coldness, and rubbed his face therewith.\nوَاَعَانَتْهُ مَلَاۤئِكَتُكَ عَلٰى غُسْلِهٖ وَتَجْهِيْزِهٖ\nWA A'AANAT-HU MALAA'IKATUKA A'LAA GHUSLIHEE WA TAJHEEZIH\nAnd Your angels helped him bathe and prepare his body for burial.\nوَصَلَّى عَلَيْهِ وَوَارٰى شَخْصَهٗ\nWA SALLAA A'LAYHI WA WAARAA SHAKHSAH\nHe then performed (the ritual) prayer for him and buried his body,\nوَقَضٰى دَيْنَهٗ وَاَنْجَزَ وَعْدَهٗ\nWA QADAA DAYNAHOO WA ANJAZA WA'DAH\nsettled his debts, fulfilled his promises,\nوَلَزِمَ عَهْدَهٗ وَاحْتَذٰى مِثَالَهٗ\nWA LAZIMA A'HDAHOO WAHTADHAA MITHAALAH\nkept his covenant, followed his example,\nوَحَفِظَ وَصِيَّتَهٗ\nWA HAFIZA WASIYYATAH\nand abode by his will.\nوَحِيْنَ وَجَدَ اَنْصَارًا نَهَضَ مُسْتَقِلًّا بِاَعْبَاۤءِ الْخِلَافَةِ\nWA HEENA WAJADA ANSAARAN NAHADA MUSTAQILLAN BI-A'BAA'IL KHILAAFAH\nWhen he could find supporters, he undertook the burdens of the position of leadership (caliphate)\nمُضْطَلِعًا بِاَثْقَالِ الْاِمَامَةِ\nMUDTALI'AN BI-ATHQAALIL IMAAMAH\nand assumed the loads of Imamate.\nفَنَصَبَ رَايَةَ الْهُدٰى فِيْ عِبَادِكَ\nFANASABA RAAYATAL HUDAA FEE I'BAADIK\nHe thus hoisted the flag of true guidance among Your servants,\nوَنَشَرَ ثَوْبَ الْاَمْنِ فِيْ بِلَادِكَ\nWA NASHARA THAWBAL AMNI FEE BILAADIK\nspread the dress of security in Your lands,\nوَبَسَطَ الْعَدْلَ فِيْ بَرِيَّتِكَ\nWA BASATAL A'DLA FEE BARIYYATIK\nextended justice among Your creatures,\nوَحَكَمَ بِكِتَابِكَ فِيْ خَلِيْقَتِكَ\nWA HAKAMA BIKITAABIKA FEE KHALEEQATIK\njudged according to Your Book among Your beings,\nوَاَقَامَ الْحُدُوْدَ وَقَمَعَ الْجُحُوْدَ\nWA AQAAMAL HUDOODA WA QAMA'AL JUHOOD\nexecuted the laws, suppressed unbelief,\nوَقَوَّمَ الزَّيْغَ وَسَكَّنَ الْغَمْرَةَ\nWA QAWWAMAZ ZAYGHA WA SAKKANAL GHAMRAH\nrectified the deviation, calmed the turmoil,\nوَاَبَادَ الْفَتْرَةَ وَسَدَّ الْفُرْجَةَ\nWA ABAADAL FATRATA WA SADDAL FURJAH\neradicated lethargy, blocked the gap,\nوَقَتَلَ النَّاكِثَةَ وَالْقَاسِطَةَ وَالْمَارِقَةَ\nWA QATALAN NAAKITHATA WAL QAASITATA WAL MAARIQAH\nkilled the breakers of allegiance, the wrongdoers, and the apostates,\nوَلَمْ يَزَلْ عَلٰى مِنْهَاجِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nWA LAM YAZAL A'LAA MINHAAJI RASOOLILLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nand kept on following the course of Allah’s Messenger, peace be upon him and his Household,\nوَوَتِيْرَتِهٖ وَلُطْفِ شَاكِلَتِهٖ وَجَمَالِ سِيْرَتِهٖ\nWA WATEERATIHEE WA LUTFI SHAAKILATIHEE WA JAMAALI SEERATIH\nhis tradition, his excellent pattern, and his superb practice,\nمُقْتَدِيًا بِسُنَّتِهٖ مُتَعَلِّقًا بِهِمَّتِهٖ\nMUQTADIYAN BISUNNATIHEE MUTA'ALLIQAN BIHIMMATIH\nimitating his convention, holding fast to his morale,\nمُبَاشِرًا لِطَرِيْقَتِهٖ وَاَمْثِلَتُهٗ نَصْبُ عَيْنَيْهِ\nMUBAASHIRAN LITAREEQATIHEE WA AMTHILATUHOO NASBU A'YNAYH\ncopying his way (of treating matters), with the Prophet’s deeds always before his eyes;\nيَحْمِلُ عِبَادَكَ عَلَيْهَا وَيَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلَيْهَا\nYAHMILU I'BAADAKA A'LAYHAA WA YAD'OOHUM ILAYHAA\nhe urged Your servants to copy these deeds and invited them to imitate them,\nاِلٰى اَنْ خُضِبَتْ شَيْبَتُهٗ مِنْ دَمِ رَاْسِهٖ\nILAA AN KHUDIBAT SHAYBATUHOO MIN DAMI RA'SIH\nuntil his white beard was dyed with the blood of his head.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَكَمَا لَمْ يُؤْثِرْ فِيْ طَاعَتِكَ شَكًّا عَلٰى يَقِيْنٍ\nALLAAHUMMA FAKAMAA LAM YU'THIR FEE TAA'ATIKA SHAKKAN A'LAA YAQEEN\nO Allah, as he never preferred a dubious matter to a certain one for the sake of obeying You\nوَلَمْ يُشْرِكْ بِكَ طَرْفَةَ عَيْنٍ\nWA LAM YUSHRIK BIKA TARFATA A'YN\nand never associated anyone with You even for a twinkling of an eye,\nصَلِّ عَلَيْهِ صَلَاةً زَاكِيَةً نَامِيَةً\nSALLI A'LAYHI SALAATAN ZAAKIYATAN NAAMIYAH\nplease send upon him growing and increasing blessings\nيَلْحَقُ بِهَا دَرَجَةَ النُّبُوَّةِ فِيْ جَنَّتِكَ\nYALHAQU BIHAA DARAJATAN NUBUWWATI FEE JANNATIK\ndue to which he may join the position of Prophethood in Your Paradise,\nوَبَلِّغْهُ مِنَّا تَحِيَّةً وَسَلَامًا\nWA BALLIGH-HU MINNAA TAHIYYATAN WA SALAAMAA\nand (please) convey our greetings and compliments to him,\nوَاٰتِنَا مِنْ لَدُنْكَ فِيْ مُوَالَاتِهٖ فَضْلًا وَاِحْسَانًا\nWA AATINAA MIN LADUNKA FEE MUWAALAATIHEE FADLAN WA IHSAANAA\nand, on account of our allegiance to his leadership, please grant us from You favor, kindness,\nوَمَغْفِرَةً وَرِضْوَانًا\nWA MAGHFIRATAN WA RIDWAANAA\nforgiveness, and pleasure.\nاِنَّكَ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْجَسِيْمِ\nINNAKA DHUL FADLIL JASEEM\nYou are verily the Lord of enormous favor.\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\n(Please do that) by Your mercy, O most merciful of all those who show mercy.\nPlace your right cheek on the tomb, then your left. Then face the qiblah, pray the two-unit ziyarat prayer and ask Allah for whatever you wish.\nThen recite the [Tasbih al-Zahra](I9) and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ بَشَّرْتَنِيْ عَلٰى لِسَانِ نَبِيِّكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA BASHSHARTANEE A'LAA LISAANI NABIYYIK\nO Allah, You have conveyed to me glad tidings through Your Prophet\nوَرَسُوْلِكَ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nWA RASOOLIKA MUHAMMADIN SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nand Messenger Muhammad, Your blessings be upon him and his Household,\nفَقُلْتَ وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا\nFAQULTA WA BASHSHIRIL LADHEENA AAMANOO\nas You said, “And give good news to those who believe\nاَنَّ لَهُمْ قَدَمَ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ\nANNA LAHUM QADAMA SIDQIN I'NDA RABBIHIM\nthat theirs is a footing of firmness with their Lord.”\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَاِنِّيْ مُؤْمِنٌ بِجَمِيْعِ اَنْبِيَاۤئِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA WA INNEE MU'MINUN BIJAMEE'I ANBIYAA'IK\nO Allah, I indeed believe in all Your Prophets\nوَرُسُلِكَ صَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِمْ\nWA RUSULIKA SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHIM\nand Messengers, Your blessings be upon them.\nفَلَا تَقِفْنِيْ بَعْدَ مَعْرِفَتِهِمْ\nFALAA TAQIFNEE BA'DA MA'RIFATIHIM\nSo, (please) do not cause me, after my recognition of them,\nمَوْقِفًا تَفْضَحُنِيْ فِيْهِ عَلٰى رُءُوْسِ الْاَشْهَادِ\nMAWQIFAN TAFDAHUNEE FEEHI A'LAA RU'OOSIL ASH-HAAD\nto be in a situation due to which You expose me in the presence of the Witnesses;\nبَلْ قِفْنِيْ مَعَهُمْ\nBAL QIFNEE MA'AHUM\nrather, (please) include me with them\nوَتَوَفَّنِيْ عَلَى التَّصْدِيْقِ بِهِمْ\nWA TAWAFFANEE A'LAT TASDEEQI BIHIM\nand make me die while I give them credence.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَاَنْتَ خَصَصْتَهُمْ بِكَرَامَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA WA ANTA KHASASTAHUM BIKARAAMATIK\nO Allah, You have also bestowed upon them exclusive honor from You\nوَاَمَرْتَنِيْ بِاتِّبَاعِهِمْ\nWA AMARTANEE BITTIBAA'IHIM\nand You have ordered me to follow them.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَاِنِّيْ عَبْدُكَ وَزَاۤئِرُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA WA INNEE A'BDUKA WA ZAA'IRUK\nO Allah, I am Your slave and visitor,\nمُتَقَرِّبًا اِلَيْكَ بِزِيَارَةِ اَخِيْ رَسُوْلِكَ\nMUTAQARRIBAN ILAYKA BIZIYAARATI AKHEE RASOOLIK\nseeking Your nearness through visiting the brother of Your Messenger.\nوَعَلٰى كُلِّ مَاْتِيٍّ وَمَزُوْرٍ حَقٌّ لِمَنْ اَتَاهُ وَزَارَهٗ\nWA A'LAA KULLI MA'TIYYIN WA MAZOORIN HAQQUN LIMAN ATAAHU WA ZAARAH\nIndeed, each visited person is expected to pay attention to his duty towards the one who visits and comes to him.\nوَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ مَاْتِيٍّ وَاَكْرَمُ مَزُوْرٍ\nWA ANTA KHAYRU MA'TIYYIN WA AKRAMU MAZOOR\nAnd You are the Best One to Whom one may come and You are the most Generous One to be visited;\nفَاَسْاَلُكَ يَاۤ اَللّٰهُ يَا رَحْمٰنُ يَا رَحِيْمُ\nFA-AS'ALUKA YAA ALLAAHU YAA RAHMAANU YAA RAHEEM\nI therefore beseech You, O Allah, O All-beneficent, O All-merciful,\nيَا جَوَادُ يَا مَاجِدُ يَا اَحَدُ يَا صَمَدُ\nYAA JAWAADU YAA MAAJIDU YAA AHADU YAA SAMAD\nO All-magnanimous, O All-glorious, O One, O Besought of all,\nيَا مَنْ لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُوْلَدْ\nYAA MAN LAM YALID WA LAM YOOLAD\nO He Who never begets nor is He begotten,\nوَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ كُفُوًا اَحَدٌ\nWA LAM YAKUN LAHOO KUFUWAN AHAD\nand the like of Whom is none,\nوَلَمْ يَتَّخِذْ صَاحِبَةً وَلَا وَلَدًا\nWA LAM YATTAKHIDH SAAHIBATAN WA LAA WALADAA\nand Who has not betaken wife or child,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\n(I beseech You) to send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاَنْ تَجْعَلَ تُحْفَتَكَ اِيَّايَ مِنْ زِيَارَتِيْ اَخَا رَسُوْلِكَ\nWA AN TAJ'ALA TUHFATAKA IYYAAYA MIN ZIYAARATEE AKHAA RASOOLIK\nto choose the gift that You present to me on account of my visiting Your Messenger’s brother\nفَكَاكَ رَقَبَتِيْ مِنَ النَّارِ\nFAKAAKA RAQABATEE MINAN NAAR\nto be the release of my neck from Hellfire,\nوَاَنْ تَجْعَلَنِيْ مِمَّنْ يُسَارِعُ فِي الْخَيْرَاتِ\nWA AN TAJ'ALANEE MIMMAN YUSAARI'U FIL KHAYRAAT\nto include me with those who strive with one another in hastening to good deeds\nوَيَدْعُوْكَ رَغَبًا وَرَهَبًا\nWA YAD'OOKA RAGHABAN WA RAHABAA\nand those who call on You with love and reverence,\nوَتَجْعَلَنِيْ لَكَ مِنَ الْخَاشِعِيْنَ\nWA TAJ'ALANEE LAKA MINAL KHAASHI'EEN\nand to make me of those who are humble before You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ مَنَنْتَ عَلَيَّ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA MANANTA A'LAYY\nO Allah, You have indeed conferred upon me\nبِزِيَارَةِ مَوْلَايَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ وَوِلَايَتِهٖ وَمَعْرِفَتِهٖ\nBIZIYAARATI MAWLAAYA A'LIYYIBNI ABEE TAALIBIN WA WILAAYATIHEE WA MA'RIFATIH\nthe favor of visiting my master ‘Ali the son of Abu-Talib, and of being loyal to his (Divinely commissioned) leadership and recognizing him;\nفَاجْعَلْنِيْ مِمَّنْ يَنْصُرُهٗ وَيَنْتَصِرُ بِهٖ\nFAJ'ALNEE MIMMAN YANSURUHOO WA YANTASIRU BIH\nso, (please) make me of those who support him and are victorious through him,\nوَمُنَّ عَلَيَّ بِنَصْرِكَ لِدِيْنِكَ\nWA MUNNA A'LAYYA BINASRIKA LIDEENIK\nand (please) bestow me with the favor of making me support Your religion.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَاجْعَلْنِيْ مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA WAJ'ALNEE MIN SHEE'ATIH\nO Allah, (please) include me with the adherents of him\nوَتَوَفَّنِيْ عَلٰى دِيْنِهٖ\nWA TAWAFFANEE A'LAA DEENIH\nand cause me to die following his doctrine.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَوْجِبْ لِيْ مِنَ الرَّحْمَةِ وَالرِّضْوَانِ\nALLAAHUMMA AWJIB LEE MINAR RAHMATI WAR RIDWAAN\nO Allah, (please) cause me to deserve mercy, pleasure,\nوَالْمَغْفِرَةِ وَالْاِحْسَانِ وَالرِّزْقِ الْوَاسِعِ الْحَلَالِ الطَّيِّبِ\nWAL MAGHFIRATI WAL IHSAANI WAR RIZQIL WAASI'IL HALAALIT TAYYIB\nforgiveness, favor, and sustenance that is growing, legally gotten, and pleasant,\nمَا اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nMAA ANTA AHLUHOO YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nas befits You, O most merciful of all those who show mercy!\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nAll praise be to Allah the Lord of the worlds.",
  "merits": "Shaykh al-Mufid, Sayyid Ibn Tawus and al-Shahid report this ziyarat of Imam Ali (a.s.) for the day of the Mab'ath, the twenty-seventh of Rajab, and the night before it.\n\nMafatih al-Jinan gives three forms of ziyarat for this day. The first is al-Ziyarah al-Rajabiyyah, [Ziyarat Rajabiyah](X4); the author of al-Mazar al-Qadim and Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Mashhadi count it among the forms special to the night of the Mab'ath, and add that after it one may offer a two-unit prayer and ask Allah for one's needs. The second begins \"Peace be upon the father of the Imams and the essence of Prophethood\"; Allamah al-Majlisi counts it as the seventh of the ziyarat for any time in his Tuhfat al-Za'ir, but the author of al-Mazar al-Qadim names it for the day of the Mab'ath, and Shaykh Abbas Qummi adds it to this day's forms in his Hadiyyat al-Za'ir. The third is this one.\n\nImam Ali (a.s.) also has a ziyarat of his own at Najaf for the Prophet's (s.a.w.a.) birthday, the seventeenth of Rabi al-Awwal.\n\nIt is narrated through an authoritative chain that when Imam Ali (a.s.) was martyred, al-Khidr (a.s.) hurried to his house weeping, stopped at the door and said: \"May Allah have mercy upon you, O Abu'l-Hasan. You were the first of all to accept Islam, the most sincere of all in faith, the most confident, the most Allah-fearing...\" and went on to name many of his virtues. As his words closely resemble this ziyarat, Shaykh Abbas Qummi suggests reciting them as a ziyarat on the day of Imam Ali's martyrdom; he records them in full in his Hadiyyat al-Za'ir."
}
